@startuml fig2_architecture
' Diagram 2 of the ISO/IEC 7498-1 pattern: the architecture inside an open
' system.
'
' Conventions: shared/FIGURES.md. Flat boxes, no namespace prefixes, no clause
' numbers, orthogonal edges, nothing explanatory inside the drawing.
'
' What it shows: how an open system is built out of subsystems, one per layer,
' what sits inside a subsystem, and the two relations that make a stack a stack
' rather than seven unrelated things.
'
' Two relations run in different directions on purpose. providesService goes
' up, from an entity to the layer above it, and employsProtocol goes sideways,
' between the entities of one layer in different systems. That is the whole
' architecture of clause 5.2 in two edges.
'
' peerEntity is drawn as a self-edge, since a peer is an entity like any other.
' The standard has peers sit at the same layer, 5.2.1.3, and the pattern states
' no axiom for it: nothing here stops a model from relating two across layers.
'
' The layer catalogue is supplied separately in ISO7498-instances.ttl. A model
' taking only the pattern gets the class without the seven layers.
'
' Left out on purpose:
'  - the communication itself and what it promises: diagram 1
'  - the data units passing through: diagram 3
'  - isSublayerOf, which divides a layer into sublayers, 5.3.1.1. It is in the
'    pattern and no test case uses it, and drawn here its edge crosses the
'    entity box for a relation the diagram is not about.

skinparam backgroundColor transparent
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam nodesep 25
skinparam ranksep 45
skinparam padding 3
skinparam ArrowColor #1A2733
skinparam ArrowFontSize 13
skinparam ArrowFontColor #1A2733
hide empty members
hide circle
skinparam class {
  BackgroundColor #FCEFC7
  BorderColor #C9A227
  FontColor #1A2733
  FontSize 14
  BorderThickness 1
}

class OpenSystem
class Subsystem
class Entity
class ServiceAccessPoint
class Service
class Protocol

class Layer {
  dataProp: layerNumber
  «enum»
  ApplicationLayer
  PresentationLayer
  SessionLayer
  TransportLayer
  NetworkLayer
  DataLinkLayer
  PhysicalLayer
}

OpenSystem --> "*" Subsystem : hasSubsystem
Subsystem  --> "*" Entity    : hasEntity
Subsystem  --> "1" Layer     : atLayer

Entity --> "*" Service  : providesService
Entity --> "*" Protocol : employsProtocol

' Routed left: the self-edge is drawn on the right by default, which is where
' the layer catalogue stands, and its label landed on that box.
Entity -left-> "*" Entity : peerEntity

ServiceAccessPoint --> "*" Entity : attachedTo

@enduml
